Subject: [PATCH] debian: Add nativehdr6 changelog entry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Summarise the HLG and target-aware tone mapping batch: the HLG transfer
function, its shared luminance validity check and its Wayland and CICP
mappings; the source target color volume from mastering metadata and
content light levels, with extended_target_volume advertised and the
single effective peak definition, unknown for extended-range content
without declarations; and BT.2390 highlight compression toward a
declared output target peak, with matching direct scanout and hardware
cursor plane decisions, exact transform caching and the output's
reference white in whole cd/m². The new exported symbols were added to
the symbols file with their commits, at 51.0-1ubuntu3+nativehdr6~.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
---
 debian/changelog | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/debian/changelog b/debian/changelog
index 1035f1c..9fa163d 100644
--- a/debian/changelog
+++ b/debian/changelog
@@ -1,3 +1,38 @@
+mutter (51.0-1ubuntu3+nativehdr6) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium
+
+  * Add the HLG transfer function (Rec. ITU-R BT.2100-2): decode with black
+    level lift, inverse OETF and the luminance-dependent OOTF in the source
+    primaries (system gamma 1.2 * 1.111^log2 (Lw / 1000)), with its exact
+    inverse for HLG destinations; accept and advertise
+    transfer_function.hlg, and map CICP transfer characteristics 18. HLG
+    luminances whose black level lift would exceed 0.5 are refused by one
+    shared check: the Wayland creator fails them with 'unsupported'.
+  * Keep a private target color volume in parametric color states: accept
+    and validate mastering display primaries and luminance, MaxCLL and
+    MaxFALL from Wayland clients, advertise set_mastering_display_primaries
+    and extended_target_volume (target primaries are never used to map
+    gamut), and let the declaration take part in color state equality,
+    hashing and image description identity without adding conversions
+    between otherwise equal encodings. The effective source peak is the
+    lowest of the encoding's range, the mastering peak and MaxCLL; for
+    extended-range linear encodings, without either declaration, it is
+    unknown.
+  * Compress highlights toward a firmware-declared output target peak with
+    the Report ITU-R BT.2390 EETF on max (R, G, B), without a black level
+    lift, once, in the surface to blending transform, only when the
+    source's known effective peak exceeds the target after reference-white
+    scaling. Direct scanout is refused exactly when that mapping applies,
+    by the predicate the renderer uses; the hardware cursor plane is not
+    used for a cursor that would be mapped, re-evaluated on the first frame
+    after a view's color states change.
+    Without a declared peak nothing changes. Color transforms are cached by
+    exact color state identity, and the output reference luminance is kept
+    in whole cd/m², as published.
+  * KMS HDR metadata is unchanged. Source candidate only; runtime and
+    package qualification pending.
+
+ -- Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
+
 mutter (51.0-1ubuntu3+nativehdr5) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium
 
   * Accept signed custom primaries for encoding gamuts within [-16, 16]
